# AISDF workflow rules

- Read AISDF governance and the requested WF-007–WF-012 procedure before acting.
- Use the portable `tools/aisdf.py` runtime and persist artifacts under `.aisdf/`.
- Keep concept challenge, specification drafting, review, and implementation as separate gated stages.
- Never claim independent review unless fresh context isolation is evidenced. If unavailable, report `NON_INDEPENDENT` or `BLOCKED`.
- Do not modify application source before explicit human approval of the specification and exact file allowlist.
- Preserve dissent and all review findings; resolutions require evidence.
- Run tests and drift checks after implementation; report limitations honestly.
